  <h2>Narrative Summary</h2>
  <p>The Collaborative Advocate Foundation (TCAF) is in its startup phase, fully funded by founder contributions from Dr. Terry Flood. All funds have been invested in building the organization's technology infrastructure — a 24-platform ecosystem serving Central Texas communities through workforce development, health equity, benefits navigation, and social determinants of health data intelligence.</p>

  <p>TCAF operates without paid staff during this phase. Dr. Flood serves as uncompensated Founder and CEO, contributing his expertise in healthcare administration, implementation science, and community development. The organization's primary assets are its technology platforms, proprietary RPLICE implementation science engine, curriculum content, and community relationships — including Dr. Flood's position on the Pflugerville ISD School Health Advisory Council (SHAC).</p>

  <p>TCAF is actively pursuing grant funding to transition from founder-funded operations to sustainable programmatic delivery. Current applications in progress include workforce development grants (Texas Workforce Commission), benefits enrollment infrastructure (St. David's Foundation), and nonclinical youth mental health workforce development (Rare Impact Fund).</p>

  <h2>Key Organizational Assets (Non-Financial)</h2>
  <table>
  <tr><th style="width:40%">Asset</th><th style="width:60%">Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>24-Platform Technology Ecosystem</td><td>Live, operational platforms spanning workforce development, health equity, benefits navigation, education, veteran services, and community data intelligence</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RPLICE Implementation Science Engine</td><td>Proprietary platform operationalizing CFIR 2.0, RE-AIM, EPIS, and other frameworks for program fidelity monitoring and continuous improvement</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Workforce Readiness Curriculum</td><td>20 lessons across 5 modules with culturally responsive content, live and serving youth through PfISD partnership</td></tr>
  <tr><td>GIS Community Intelligence</td><td>Integration with 8 federal data sources (CDC PLACES, SVI, Census ACS, USDA, FBI, HUD, SAMHSA, BLS) for census tract-level community analysis</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Community Relationships</td><td>Pflugerville ISD SHAC membership, coalition partnerships across Central Texas</td></tr>
  </table>

